WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.333
Hi everyone,
I'm Scarlett Johansson

00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:03.375
and I'm here with
my Black Widow co-stars,

00:00:03.417 --> 00:00:05.417
Florence Pugh
and David Harbour.

00:00:05.458 --> 00:00:06.750
Back together again.

00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:08.417
♪

00:00:08.458 --> 00:00:09.750
(exclaims)

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:12.208
We're gathered here today
to look at your Tweets

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.291
and guess which one of us
the Tweet is about.

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:16.792
-Let's do this.
-"Can we talk about

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:20.625
the immaculate
music taste ____ has."

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:21.917
I know that's not me.

00:00:21.959 --> 00:00:23.875
It's probably, like, Florence.

00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:26.792
But "immaculate" is a bit
too squeaky clean.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.583
(all exclaim)

00:00:28.625 --> 00:00:30.834
I knew it, it's so cool, right?

00:00:30.875 --> 00:00:34.166
Okay, "Wait, I just found out
____ is a twin.

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:35.917
Was this common knowledge?"

00:00:35.959 --> 00:00:37.208
Scarlett,
it's about Scarlett.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.834
Yeah, Scarlett,
she's the twin.

00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:39.834
Me, me, me, me.

00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:42.166
"Just came here to state
my excitement

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.208
about ____ doing
a Russian accent

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.375
in the Black Widow trailer.

00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:46.625
I'm in."

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.917
-Rachel?
-I was gonna say Rachel too.

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:49.959
Aw, come on.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.250
(laughter)

00:00:51.291 --> 00:00:54.000
Come on, you're gonna
give this one to Rachel Weisz?

00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:56.291
None of you are excited
about my Russian accent.

00:00:56.333 --> 00:00:57.375
-I think it's me.
-I imitate it all the time!

00:00:57.417 --> 00:00:59.500
I'm gonna go double down on me.

00:00:59.542 --> 00:01:01.500
Who is it?

00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:02.458
-David Harbour.
-Yes!

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.333
Oh!

00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:06.375
Justice, vindication.

00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.792
Sorry, we can move on.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.000
(laughing)

00:01:09.041 --> 00:01:10.542
I have a lot of energy.

00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:13.125
"I'm obsessed with
_____'s tea tutorial."

00:01:13.166 --> 00:01:14.291
That's gotta be Florence.

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:15.542
Yeah, that's me. That's me.

00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:17.333
Do you make like
cups of tea and stuff?

00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.583
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:18.625 --> 00:01:20.750
Do you put the milk in first
like the British--

00:01:20.792 --> 00:01:23.792
No! That is crazy.

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:25.625
Is that a serious question?

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.333
"Can you believe it,
the Earth is a billion years old

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:31.375
and you manage to live
the same time as..."

00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:33.708
Yeah, that's Scarlett,
because I feel that too.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.834
Me too.

00:01:34.875 --> 00:01:35.917
What's that supposed to mean?

00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:38.750
I don't understand this Tweet.

00:01:38.792 --> 00:01:40.834
Basically, someone's
really happy that they're living

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:42.542
in the same period of time
as you.

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:45.583
Oh, right, as opposed
to like medieval times?

00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:47.500
"Why does ____'s
New York loft

00:01:47.542 --> 00:01:49.250
look like my entire Pinterest?"

00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:50.375
That's David.

00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:51.875
Yeah, that's David.

00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:53.917
And, you know, that's
like a 13-year-old girl

00:01:53.959 --> 00:01:56.083
who's saying that.
I showed that to my designer.

00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:57.708
I was like, "Here.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.583
This is Allison
from junior high's Pinterest.

00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:03.458
I want it to look
exactly like that."

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.708
♪

